# Allowlist, not a blocklist: ignore EVERYTHING, then let in only what the images need.
# A blocklist fails open (a new secret file or a 2 GB folder ships until someone notices);
# an allowlist fails closed (a missing file breaks the build, loudly).
*

# The uv workspace: root manifest + lock, and every member's manifest (uv needs all members
# to resolve the workspace, even those it doesn't install, e.g. evals).
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!evals/pyproject.toml

# Python sources the image runs (api incl. Alembic migrations, the MCP servers, the simulator)
!api/
!simulator/
!mcp/
# Plant layout (seed, simulator) and the knowledge base (ingest)
!data/
# The dashboard (web.Dockerfile, 10.6′a); its node_modules and build output are excluded below
!web/

# ...minus what is inside those folders but never belongs in an image
**/tests/
**/__pycache__/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.venv/
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
# Defense in depth: no env file, wherever it sits, ever reaches the build context.
**/.env
**/.env.*
